      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-58dcc8093664",
          "exact": "The ARM architecture is a load–store architecture. Uniform 16 × 32-bit register file (including the program counter, stack pointer and the link register). Fixed instruction width of 32 bits to ease decoding and pipelining, at the cost of decreased code density. Later, the Thumb instruction set added 16-bit instructions and increased code density."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-58dcc8093664",
          "subject": "The ARM architecture",
          "predicate": "has",
          "object": "load–store design; uniform 16 × 32-bit register file incl. PC/SP/LR; fixed 32-bit instruction width at cost of code density; later Thumb 16-bit instructions increasing code density"
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "WIKI-001",
        "EVD-001",
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "引文支撑 claim 的四个组成部分：'load–store architecture'（[0,50]）；'Uniform 16 × 32-bit register file (including the program counter, stack pointer and the link register)'（[51,154]）；'Fixed instruction width of 32 bits to ease decoding and pipelining, at the cost of decreased code density'（[155,261]）；'the Thumb instruction set added 16-bit instructions and increased code density'（[262,348]）。但 claim 中'多数指令单周期执行'在引文全段无对应文本：引文通篇未提及单周期/cycle 相关表述，该断言无证据支持，故为部分支持。",
